FORM K-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: the-castle.
FILED BY: the land surveyor K, who was sent for and is still waiting to be received.

OFF THE RECORD: Can it run DOOM? It can run this: a first-person
OFF THE RECORD: raycaster, Wolfenstein-grade, over a village map held
OFF THE RECORD: in a schedule of strings. The camera is a direction
OFF THE RECORD: vector and a plane vector, fixed point, scaled by
OFF THE RECORD: 1000; each of the 15 screen columns casts one ray
OFF THE RECORD: through the plane and marches it until masonry; the
OFF THE RECORD: march parameter is the perpendicular distance, so the
OFF THE RECORD: walls stand straight without correction. Twenty-one
OFF THE RECORD: rows of ASCII per frame, walls shaded by distance and
OFF THE RECORD: by facing (south-facing stone catches the light,
OFF THE RECORD: east-facing stone does not; the Court has been told
OFF THE RECORD: this is called rendering).
OFF THE RECORD:
OFF THE RECORD: PROCLAIM is the framebuffer, one proclamation per
OFF THE RECORD: frame. AWAIT SUMMONS is the controls: w/s to stride,
OFF THE RECORD: a/d to turn, q to give up, which is the only ending
OFF THE RECORD: offered. trial observe is the display. The
OFF THE RECORD: trigonometry is incorporated from the canon.
OFF THE RECORD:
OFF THE RECORD: The village is 16 cells square. The walls marked #
OFF THE RECORD: are the village; the walls marked C are the Castle,
OFF THE RECORD: which stands in the middle, has an interior, and has
OFF THE RECORD: no door. You may approach it. That is all.
OFF THE RECORD:
OFF THE RECORD: Against a live broker every instruction is a Kafka
OFF THE RECORD: transaction, so this is DOOM at minutes per frame,
OFF THE RECORD: every frame of it replayable, bit for bit, forever.
OFF THE RECORD: In chambers (trial test) it renders instantly, which
OFF THE RECORD: the deposition beside it demonstrates.

INCORPORATE BY REFERENCE statutes-of-trigonometry.

THE EXHIBIT OF impact, COMPRISING reach AND material AND facing.

ARTICLE 1.
    OFF THE RECORD: the village, surveyed once for the record, one
    OFF THE RECORD: string per row of cells. The game never shows
    OFF THE RECORD: this document; the game is what it looks like
    OFF THE RECORD: from inside it. K. begins at (8.5, 14.5), in the
    OFF THE RECORD: square before the corridor, facing north; north
    OFF THE RECORD: is bearing 90, because east is 0 and the map
    OFF THE RECORD: counts its rows downward, like every official
    OFF THE RECORD: document.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT village IS A SCHEDULE COMPRISING
        "################" AND
        "#..............#" AND
        "#..##....##....#" AND
        "#...#.....#....#" AND
        "#...#..........#" AND
        "#......CCCC....#" AND
        "#..##..C..C..#.#" AND
        "#..#...C..C..#.#" AND
        "#..#...CCCC..#.#" AND
        "#..............#" AND
        "#.####....####.#" AND
        "#....#....#....#" AND
        "#....#....#....#" AND
        "#..............#" AND
        "#..............#" AND
        "################".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT sines IS THE FINDING OF the-table-of-sines.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT px IS 8500.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT py IS 14500.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT ang IS 90.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT day IS 0.
    PETITION THE OFFICE OF the-compass.

ARTICLE 2.
    OFF THE RECORD: one proclamation, one frame.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT day IS day PLUS 1.
    PROCLAIM THE FINDING OF the-rendered-frame.

ARTICLE 3.
    OFF THE RECORD: the controls. Input is not requested; it is served.
    AWAIT SUMMONS, FILED UNDER key.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT key IS THE TRANSCRIPT OF key.
    SHOULD key EQUAL "w", REFER TO ARTICLE 4.
    SHOULD key EQUAL "s", REFER TO ARTICLE 5.
    SHOULD key EQUAL "a", REFER TO ARTICLE 6.
    SHOULD key EQUAL "d", REFER TO ARTICLE 7.
    SHOULD key EQUAL "q", REFER TO ARTICLE 8.
    OFF THE RECORD: any other summons is noted, retained, and disregarded.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 3.

ARTICLE 4.
    PETITION THE OFFICE OF stride WITH 1.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 2.

ARTICLE 5.
    PETITION THE OFFICE OF stride WITH -1.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 2.

ARTICLE 6.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT ang IS (ang PLUS 115) NOTWITHSTANDING 120.
    PETITION THE OFFICE OF the-compass.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 2.

ARTICLE 7.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT ang IS (ang PLUS 5) NOTWITHSTANDING 120.
    PETITION THE OFFICE OF the-compass.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 2.

ARTICLE 8.
    PROCLAIM "K. turns back for the night. The Castle has not received him, and the record shows he was here.".
    ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.

OFF THE RECORD: the offices. Positions are in thousandths of a cell;
OFF THE RECORD: a cell's coordinates are its position apportioned
OFF THE RECORD: among 1000, and the map is consulted one character at
OFF THE RECORD: a time, because the map is a document like everything
OFF THE RECORD: else here.

THE OFFICE OF the-cell, CONCERNING cx AND cy.
    REMAND WITH AN EXCERPT OF (THE ITEM AT cy IN village) FROM cx TO cx.

THE OFFICE OF the-compass.
    OFF THE RECORD: consulted whenever the bearing changes. The
    OFF THE RECORD: direction is where K. faces; the plane is the
    OFF THE RECORD: camera, perpendicular to it, 660 per mille wide,
    OFF THE RECORD: which the surveyors call a 67 degree field of view.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT dirx IS THE FINDING OF cosine REGARDING ang AND sines.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT diry IS THE FINDING OF sine REGARDING ang AND sines.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT planex IS 0 LESS (diry TIMES 660) APPORTIONED AMONG 1000.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT planey IS (dirx TIMES 660) APPORTIONED AMONG 1000.

THE OFFICE OF stride, CONCERNING sign.
    OFF THE RECORD: half a cell per step, each axis cleared separately,
    OFF THE RECORD: so K. slides along walls instead of arguing with them.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT mx IS px PLUS (sign TIMES dirx) APPORTIONED AMONG 2.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT my IS py PLUS (sign TIMES diry) APPORTIONED AMONG 2.
    SHOULD (THE FINDING OF the-cell REGARDING mx APPORTIONED AMONG 1000 AND py APPORTIONED AMONG 1000) EQUAL ".", LET IT BE RECORDED THAT px IS mx.
    SHOULD (THE FINDING OF the-cell REGARDING px APPORTIONED AMONG 1000 AND my APPORTIONED AMONG 1000) EQUAL ".", LET IT BE RECORDED THAT py IS my.

THE OFFICE OF the-ray, CONCERNING cam.
    OFF THE RECORD: one ray, cast through the camera plane at cam
    OFF THE RECORD: per mille off center, marched a tenth of a unit
    OFF THE RECORD: at a time until masonry or twenty-four units of
    OFF THE RECORD: perpendicular distance, whichever is struck
    OFF THE RECORD: first. On arrival the ray reports which way the
    OFF THE RECORD: wall it hit was facing: if its last step crossed
    OFF THE RECORD: a column boundary and no row boundary, the stone
    OFF THE RECORD: faces east or west, and is shaded accordingly.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT rdx IS dirx PLUS (planex TIMES cam) APPORTIONED AMONG 1000.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT rdy IS diry PLUS (planey TIMES cam) APPORTIONED AMONG 1000.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT sx IS rdx APPORTIONED AMONG 10.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT sy IS rdy APPORTIONED AMONG 10.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT rx IS px.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT ry IS py.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT gone IS 0.
SECTION 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT rx IS rx PLUS sx.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT ry IS ry PLUS sy.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT gone IS gone PLUS 100.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT struck IS THE FINDING OF the-cell REGARDING rx APPORTIONED AMONG 1000 AND ry APPORTIONED AMONG 1000.
    SHOULD struck DIFFER FROM ".", REFER TO SECTION 2.
    SHOULD gone FALL SHORT OF 24000, REFER TO SECTION 1.
    REMAND WITH AN EXHIBIT OF impact WHEREIN reach IS gone AND material IS "." AND facing IS "south".
SECTION 2.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT side IS "south".
    SHOULD (rx LESS sx) APPORTIONED AMONG 1000 DIFFER FROM rx APPORTIONED AMONG 1000,
        SHOULD (ry LESS sy) APPORTIONED AMONG 1000 EQUAL ry APPORTIONED AMONG 1000,
            LET IT BE RECORDED THAT side IS "east".
    REMAND WITH AN EXHIBIT OF impact WHEREIN reach IS gone AND material IS struck AND facing IS side.

THE OFFICE OF the-glyph, CONCERNING material AND side AND reach.
    OFF THE RECORD: the village recedes @ # = - on lit faces and
    OFF THE RECORD: # = - : on shaded ones; the Castle is % and then
    OFF THE RECORD: +, and is never mistaken for the village,
    OFF THE RECORD: whatever the distance or the light.
    SHOULD material EQUAL "C", REFER TO SECTION 1.
    SHOULD side EQUAL "east", REFER TO SECTION 2.
    SHOULD reach FAIL TO EXCEED 2200, REMAND WITH "@".
    SHOULD reach FAIL TO EXCEED 4500, REMAND WITH "#".
    SHOULD reach FAIL TO EXCEED 8000, REMAND WITH "=".
    REMAND WITH "-".
SECTION 2.
    SHOULD reach FAIL TO EXCEED 2200, REMAND WITH "#".
    SHOULD reach FAIL TO EXCEED 4500, REMAND WITH "=".
    SHOULD reach FAIL TO EXCEED 8000, REMAND WITH "-".
    REMAND WITH ":".
SECTION 1.
    SHOULD side EQUAL "east", REFER TO SECTION 3.
    SHOULD reach FAIL TO EXCEED 6000, REMAND WITH "%".
    REMAND WITH "+".
SECTION 3.
    SHOULD reach FAIL TO EXCEED 3000, REMAND WITH "%".
    REMAND WITH "+".

THE OFFICE OF the-floor, CONCERNING row.
    OFF THE RECORD: the ground gains conviction as it approaches.
    SHOULD row EXCEED 6, REMAND WITH ".".
    SHOULD row EXCEED 5, REMAND WITH ",".
    REMAND WITH "`".

THE OFFICE OF the-rendered-frame.
    OFF THE RECORD: fifteen columns, one ray each, swept across the
    OFF THE RECORD: camera plane; seven rows, ceiling above,
    OFF THE RECORD: graded floor below, wall glyphs between, taller
    OFF THE RECORD: as the masonry approaches. The last line is the
    OFF THE RECORD: caption, which is also the save file.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT heights IS AN EMPTY SCHEDULE.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT glyphs IS AN EMPTY SCHEDULE.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT col IS 1.
SECTION 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT struck-ray IS THE FINDING OF the-ray REGARDING (col LESS 8) TIMES 1000 APPORTIONED AMONG 7.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT span IS THE reach ENTERED IN struck-ray.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT tall IS 7000 APPORTIONED AMONG span.
    SHOULD tall EXCEED 7, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT tall IS 7.
    SHOULD (THE material ENTERED IN struck-ray) EQUAL ".", LET IT BE RECORDED THAT tall IS 0.
    FAILING WHICH, SHOULD tall EQUAL 0, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT tall IS 1.
    ANNEX tall TO heights.
    ANNEX (THE FINDING OF the-glyph REGARDING (THE material ENTERED IN struck-ray) AND (THE facing ENTERED IN struck-ray) AND span) TO glyphs.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT col IS col PLUS 1.
    SHOULD col FAIL TO EXCEED 15, REFER TO SECTION 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT frame IS "".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT row IS 1.
SECTION 2.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT line IS "".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT col IS 1.
SECTION 3.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT tall IS THE ITEM AT col IN heights.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT lid IS (7 LESS tall) APPORTIONED AMONG 2.
    SHOULD row FAIL TO EXCEED lid, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT line IS line PLUS " ". FAILING WHICH, SHOULD row EXCEED lid PLUS tall, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT line IS line PLUS THE FINDING OF the-floor REGARDING row. FAILING WHICH, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT line IS line PLUS THE ITEM AT col IN glyphs.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT col IS col PLUS 1.
    SHOULD col FAIL TO EXCEED 15, REFER TO SECTION 3.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT frame IS frame PLUS line PLUS "\n".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT row IS row PLUS 1.
    SHOULD row FAIL TO EXCEED 7, REFER TO SECTION 2.
    REMAND WITH frame PLUS "day " PLUS THE TRANSCRIPT OF day PLUS ": K. stands at (" PLUS THE TRANSCRIPT OF (px APPORTIONED AMONG 1000) PLUS ", " PLUS THE TRANSCRIPT OF (py APPORTIONED AMONG 1000) PLUS "), bearing " PLUS THE TRANSCRIPT OF ang PLUS ".".
